# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository.
#
# This exists because the repository has already been through one round of it:
# js/data/problems.js arrived with CRLF endings while every other file used
# LF, and re-uploading it rewrote all 1051 lines for a change that altered no
# content at all. A diff that size hides whatever real change sits next to it,
# and it will happen again on any Windows checkout whose git is not set to
# convert on commit.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text and what is binary; `eol=lf` fixes
# what lands in a commit. Working directories are unaffected — an editor on
# Windows can still show and save CRLF if it wants to.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit rather than inferred, so a file that is briefly empty or oddly
# encoded cannot be mistaken for binary and slip through unnormalised.
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.webmanifest text eol=lf
